('2a11 - Inference','G2', $p$One night Anne and her friends went to watch the stars at the beach. The next day, Anne said, "I should have worn another sweater last night." Which is probably true?$p$, $c$["Her friend didn't wear an extra sweater either.","Anne will never watch stars again.","Anne was cold last night."]$c$::jsonb, 2, 3),
('2a11 - Inference','G2', $p$Bobby's friend just moved to a new house. Bobby looked at a map, and saw he had three more blocks to go. Bobby was right. Which is probably true?$p$, $c$["Bobby was driving.","Bobby hadn't been to his friend's house yet.","His friend moves all the time."]$c$::jsonb, 1, 4),
('2a11 - Inference','G2', $p$Last year at a Halloween party, everyone was having a good time. Mary went as a ghost. She danced with her friend Bob. Bob asked her, "When is Mary getting here?" Which is probably true?$p$, $c$["Bob was playing a trick on Mary.","Bob has another friend named Mary.","Mary was wearing a mask, and Bob didn't know it was her."]$c$::jsonb, 2, 5);
