-- NOTE: spot-check — "always" is also defensible here; passage word is "usually".
('2a3 - Context Clue','G2', $p$Little boys are ______ noisy and playful.$p$, $c$["never","always","usually","only"]$c$::jsonb, 2, 8),
('2a3 - Context Clue','G2', $p$My shoes and pants were ______ after playing in a puddle outside.$p$, $c$["different","wet","built","usual"]$c$::jsonb, 1, 9),
('2a3 - Context Clue','G2', $p$There are things that help us to ______ bugs from our houses.$p$, $c$["keep out","use","hide","different"]$c$::jsonb, 0, 10),
('2a3 - Context Clue','G2', $p$The penguin is an ______ bird. It cannot fly, but it is an excellent swimmer.$p$, $c$["early","unusual","always","orange"]$c$::jsonb, 1, 11),
('2a3 - Context Clue','G2', $p$Some lizards change color to match their surroundings, so their enemies cannot ______ them.$p$, $c$["hear","believe","play","see"]$c$::jsonb, 3, 12),
('2a3 - Context Clue','G2', $p$A compass is an instrument used to tell direction. Without a compass, a traveler could get ______.$p$, $c$["lost","tired","sick","map"]$c$::jsonb, 0, 13),
('2a3 - Context Clue','G2', $p$The largest animal on Earth is the whale. But, the ______ animal in the world is the giraffe. It grows to be three times as tall as humans.$p$, $c$["tallest","smallest","shortest","heaviest"]$c$::jsonb, 0, 14),
('2a3 - Context Clue','G2', $p$The toad and the frog are not as alike as people think. The toad has short, ______, and rough skin, but the frog has long, wet, and smooth skin.$p$, $c$["stiff","dry","hard","bumpy"]$c$::jsonb, 1, 15),
('2a3 - Context Clue','G2', $p$Reindeer in Alaska are like horses; they can pull heavy sleds. Human babies in Alaska drink reindeer milk. So, reindeer are also like ______.$p$, $c$["dogs","chicken","cows","cats"]$c$::jsonb, 2, 16),
('2a3 - Context Clue','G2', $p$Bees work hard to collect nectar for honey by flying from flower to flower. That is why someone working hard is said to be as ______ as a bee.$p$, $c$["lazy","busy","tired","angry"]$c$::jsonb, 1, 17),
('2a3 - Context Clue','G2', $p$A starfish is special in many ways. If an arm is lost, it can grow a new one. If a starfish is cut in two, each piece will grow into a ______ new starfish.$p$, $c$["half","other","dry","whole"]$c$::jsonb, 3, 18),
('2a3 - Context Clue','G2', $p$A wasp uses mud to build its home. It ______ mud into little balls with its legs and mouth. When the mud dries, it is so hard the wind cannot break it.$p$, $c$["digs","rolls","throws","mixes"]$c$::jsonb, 1, 19),
('2a3 - Context Clue','G2', $p$When spring comes, everything in the woods begins to ______. Many animals, which were asleep all winter, begin to move, and plants begin to flower.$p$, $c$["warm up","stop","sleep","wake up"]$c$::jsonb, 3, 20);

