-- NOTE: spot-check — passage mentions fruit being good for you, but the detail focuses on what fruits are.
('2a8 - Main Idea','G2', $p$Do you like eating fruit and vegetables? They are good for you. They come in many colors and flavors. Fruits have seeds. Most fruits grow on trees.  This story mainly tells:$p$, $c$["why a tomato is a fruit","what is good for you","what fruits are"]$c$::jsonb, 2, 1),
('2a8 - Main Idea','G2', $p$Too much light can hurt your eyes. That is why you should never look at the sun. We need light to see, but we need to be careful. When too much light gets into our eyes, we squint. This helps to keep some of the light out.  This story mainly tells:$p$, $c$["that too much light is not good for our eyes","that we squint all the time","that we should not look at the sun"]$c$::jsonb, 0, 2),
('2a8 - Main Idea','G2', $p$Sneezing is good for you. Dust and germs can get into your nose, and they can tickle. When we sneeze, we blow out a lot of air through our noses and mouths. This air blows away the dust and germs.  This story mainly tells:$p$, $c$["sneezing is useful","germs get into our nose","dust tickles"]$c$::jsonb, 0, 3),
('2a8 - Main Idea','G2', $p$Germs are so small that you need a microscope to see them. Germs are tiny living things. Some germs can make you sick. When we sneeze, we spread a lot of germs. We can also spread germs by touching things. That is why we need to wash our hands and keep our bodies clean.  This story mainly tells:$p$, $c$["how germs live","about germs and how they affect us","that we must wash our hands"]$c$::jsonb, 1, 4),
('2a8 - Main Idea','G2', $p$Mother heard noises. "Sally, what are you doing out of bed?" Sally did not answer, but she just kept walking with her eyes open. Mother called her again, but realized that Sally was sleepwalking.  This story mainly tells:$p$, $c$["that Sally did not want to answer","that Sally's mother was dreaming","that Sally was walking in her sleep"]$c$::jsonb, 2, 5),
('2a8 - Main Idea','G2', $p$Many people go to libraries. Libraries are places that have many books. You can find a book on any subject. You can read the book at the library, or you can take the book home for a few days. Many students like to study in libraries.  This story mainly tells:$p$, $c$["why libraries are useful","how many libraries there are","when the first library was opened"]$c$::jsonb, 0, 6);

